    {
      "type": 12,
      "content": {
        "version": "NotebookGroup/1.0",
        "groupType": "editable",
        "items": [
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "## Model deployments\r\n\r\n**Azure Resource Graph cannot see model deployments.** The type\r\n`microsoft.cognitiveservices/accounts/deployments` returns zero rows - this was\r\nmeasured against live deployments, not assumed.\r\n\r\nThis tab uses the **Azure Resource Manager** control plane, which returns deployments\r\nfor **one account at a time**. Click a row in the account list below to switch\r\naccounts, or use the **Model account** parameter at the top.\r\n\r\n> **Seeing an empty grid?** That usually means the selected account genuinely hosts\r\n> no models. **Microsoft Foundry (AI Services)** accounts are frequently used for\r\n> Document Intelligence, Speech or Vision rather than model hosting, so they\r\n> legitimately have zero deployments. Azure OpenAI accounts are therefore listed and\r\n> selected first. Try another account.\r\n\r\n> **Why not all accounts at once?** Workbook ARM queries only accept a single Azure\r\n> *resource* path - a tenant-level `POST /batch` is rejected with\r\n> *\"Path must be for an Azure Resource\"*, and a multi-value parameter is joined\r\n> into one malformed path rather than fanned out. Both were tested against the\r\n> live portal. The workbook therefore shows deployments for one selected account\r\n> at a time.",
              "style": "info"
            },
            "name": "mdHead"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "resources\n| where type =~ 'microsoft.cognitiveservices/accounts'\n| extend _rgs = dynamic([{ResourceGroups}])\n| where array_length(_rgs) == 0 or set_has_element(_rgs, '*') or set_has_element(_rgs, resourceGroup)\n| where kind in~ ('OpenAI','AIServices')\n| extend kindRank = iff(kind =~ 'OpenAI', 0, 1)\n| join kind=leftouter (\n    resourcecontainers\n    | where type =~ 'microsoft.resources/subscriptions'\n    | project subscriptionId, Subscription = name\n  ) on subscriptionId\n| project\n    Account = name,\n    Subscription,\n    Kind = iff(kind =~ 'OpenAI', 'Azure OpenAI', 'Microsoft Foundry (AI Services)'),\n    ['Resource group'] = resourceGroup,\n    Region = location,\n    SKU = tostring(sku.name),\n    State = tostring(properties.provisioningState),\n    Endpoint = tostring(properties.endpoint),\n    kindRank,\n    ResourceId = id\n| order by kindRank asc, Account asc\n| project-away kindRank",
              "size": 2,
              "title": "Model-hosting accounts (click a row to load its deployments)",
              "queryType": 1,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.resourcegraph/resources",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Subscriptions}"
              ],
              "showExportToExcel": true,
              "exportDefaultValue": "",
              "exportFieldName": "ResourceId",
              "gridSettings": {
                "rowLimit": 1000,
                "filter": true
              },
              "exportParameterName": "ModelAccounts"
            },
            "name": "Modelhostingaccountsclickarowtoloaditsdeployments"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "### Deployments for the selected account\r\n\r\n* **Version upgrade policy** - `NoAutoUpgrade` means the deployment will **not**\r\n  move off a retiring model version on its own. Those are your migration risks.\r\n  `OnceCurrentVersionExpired` auto-upgrades only at expiry;\r\n  `OnceNewDefaultVersionAvailable` tracks the current default.\r\n* **Content filter** - a deployment with no RAI policy is unfiltered.\r\n* **SKU** - `Standard` / `GlobalStandard` are pay-as-you-go; `ProvisionedManaged` is reserved capacity.\r\n\r\nThis grid is the authoritative response from the selected account's\r\n`/deployments` endpoint: **one row per actual deployment**. It deliberately does not\r\nmerge the model catalog into this table. Azure Workbooks supports only one join key,\r\nand composite JSONPath keys can evaluate empty in some portal runtimes, producing a\r\ncross join where every deployment is repeated for every catalog model.\r\n\r\nSelect one deployment row to load its exact lifecycle and retirement dates below.\r\nThis is a one-row regional catalog lookup on `Format.Model.Version`, not a merge, so\r\nit cannot duplicate deployment rows. Use **Model retirement** for the full calendar.\r\n\r\n**Two things to expect:**\r\n\r\n* An empty grid means the selected account has no model deployments. This is normal\r\n  for AI Services accounts used for Document Intelligence, Speech, or Vision.\r\n* **Tick exactly one account.** Azure Workbooks send an ARM query to **one Azure\r\n  resource path at a time** - `GET` and `GETARRAY` were both tested and each joins\r\n  multiple selected values into a single malformed path, and there is no\r\n  subscription-wide deployments API. Selecting several accounts will error."
            },
            "name": "mdWhat"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "{\"version\":\"ARMEndpoint/1.0\",\"method\":\"GET\",\"path\":\"{ModelAccounts}/deployments\",\"headers\":[],\"urlParams\":[{\"key\":\"api-version\",\"value\":\"2024-10-01\"}],\"batchDisabled\":false,\"transformers\":[{\"type\":\"jsonpath\",\"settings\":{\"tablePath\":\"$.value[*]\",\"columns\":[{\"path\":\"name\",\"columnid\":\"Deployment\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"id\",\"columnid\":\"Subscription\",\"columnType\":\"string\",\"substringRegexMatch\":\"^.*$\",\"substringReplace\":\"{AccountSubscriptionName}\"},{\"path\":\"id\",\"columnid\":\"Resource group\",\"columnType\":\"string\",\"substringRegexMatch\":\"^.*$\",\"substringReplace\":\"{AccountResourceGroup}\"},{\"path\":\"properties.model.name\",\"columnid\":\"Model\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"properties.model.version\",\"columnid\":\"Version\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"properties.model.format\",\"columnid\":\"Format\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"sku.name\",\"columnid\":\"SKU\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"sku.capacity\",\"columnid\":\"Capacity\",\"columnType\":\"number\"},{\"path\":\"properties.versionUpgradeOption\",\"columnid\":\"Version upgrade policy\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"properties.raiPolicyName\",\"columnid\":\"Content filter\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"properties.provisioningState\",\"columnid\":\"State\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"id\",\"columnid\":\"Resource ID\",\"columnType\":\"string\"}]}}]}",
              "size": 2,
              "title": "Model deployments",
              "queryType": 12,
              "showExportToExcel": true,
              "exportedParameters": [
                {
                  "fieldName": "Deployment",
                  "parameterName": "SelectedDeploymentName",
                  "parameterType": 1,
                  "defaultValue": ""
                },
                {
                  "fieldName": "Format",
                  "parameterName": "SelectedDeploymentFormat",
                  "parameterType": 1,
                  "defaultValue": ""
                },
                {
                  "fieldName": "Model",
                  "parameterName": "SelectedDeploymentModel",
                  "parameterType": 1,
                  "defaultValue": ""
                },
                {
                  "fieldName": "Version",
