    {
      "type": 12,
      "content": {
        "version": "NotebookGroup/1.0",
        "groupType": "editable",
        "items": [
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "## Model retirement calendar\r\n\r\nLive retirement dates straight from the Azure model catalog, via the Resource\r\nManager control plane. Nothing here is hard-coded, so the dates stay correct as\r\nMicrosoft updates them.\r\n\r\nThe catalog shown is for the **region, subscription and account kind of the account\r\ncurrently selected on the Model deployments tab** - pick a different account there to\r\nsee a different catalog.\r\n\r\n> **Why the kind filter matters.** Azure returns the catalog once **per account kind**,\r\n> so the same model is listed several times - `gpt-4.1` appears once as `OpenAI` and\r\n> again as `AIServices` with identical dates. Unfiltered, a single region returned\r\n> **167 duplicated rows**. This grid is filtered to the selected account's kind, which\r\n> removes the duplicates and shows exactly the models **that account** can run.\r\n\r\n**How to use this tab**\r\n\r\n1. Note each model + version you actually run on the **Model deployments** tab.\r\n2. Find that model + version below to get its **Inference retirement** date.\r\n3. Prioritise any deployment whose **Version upgrade policy** is `NoAutoUpgrade` -\r\n   those will not migrate themselves.\r\n\r\n**Lifecycle meanings**\r\n\r\n| Status | Meaning |\r\n| --- | --- |\r\n| `GenerallyAvailable` | Supported for production |\r\n| `Preview` | Not for production; can be retired at short notice |\r\n| `Deprecating` | Retirement scheduled - **new deployments are already blocked** |\r\n| `Deprecated` | Retired - existing deployments stop serving traffic |\r\n\r\nAzure blocks new deployments of deprecating/deprecated versions, but **existing\r\ndeployments keep running until the retirement date and then fail**. That gap is\r\nexactly what this tab is for.",
              "style": "warning"
            },
            "name": "rtHead"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "{\"version\":\"ARMEndpoint/1.0\",\"method\":\"GET\",\"path\":\"subscriptions/{AccountSubscription}/providers/Microsoft.CognitiveServices/locations/{AccountRegion}/models\",\"headers\":[],\"urlParams\":[{\"key\":\"api-version\",\"value\":\"2024-10-01\"}],\"batchDisabled\":false,\"transformers\":[{\"type\":\"jsonpath\",\"settings\":{\"tablePath\":\"$.value[?(@.kind == '{AccountKind}')]\",\"columns\":[{\"path\":\"model.name\",\"columnid\":\"Model\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"model.version\",\"columnid\":\"Version\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"model.format\",\"columnid\":\"Format\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"model.lifecycleStatus\",\"columnid\":\"Lifecycle\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"model.deprecation.inference\",\"columnid\":\"Inference retirement\",\"columnType\":\"datetime\"},{\"path\":\"model.deprecation.fineTune\",\"columnid\":\"Fine-tune retirement\",\"columnType\":\"datetime\"},{\"path\":\"kind\",\"columnid\":\"Account kind\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"model.maxCapacity\",\"columnid\":\"Max capacity\",\"columnType\":\"number\"}]}}]}",
              "size": 2,
              "title": "Model catalog and retirement dates",
              "queryType": 12,
              "showExportToExcel": true,
              "gridSettings": {
                "rowLimit": 1000,
                "filter": true,
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Lifecycle",
